- Story & Context: Marlo stood shivering beneath a tarp on the rooftop catwalk, watching brine crust the satin lapels of their salvage jacket while an unreleased vocal chop fluttered through the PA like a dying seabird. They had traded their last spare emergency breathing canister for a microchip of 2010s garage vocal stems, choosing sonic devotion over a guaranteed ride inland on the dawn evacuation barge. When Kira confronted them at the edge of the roof, threatening to cut the skiff loose and leave, Marlo merely leaned over the mixer, weeping into the granular guitar delays. Over the lush, weeping cellos, Marlo keyed the microphone to whisper their shared confession: "Tell me you love me before the water learns our names."
